stateDiagram-v2
    [*] --> Build
    Build --> Simplify: Construct interference graph<br/>from live ranges
    Simplify --> Select: Remove low-degree nodes<br/>(degree < K) to stack
    Simplify --> SpillMark: All remaining nodes<br/>have degree ≥ K
    SpillMark --> Simplify: Mark spill candidate,<br/>remove and continue
    SpillMark --> Select: No more nodes

    Select --> Coalesce: Pop nodes from stack,<br/>assign colors (optimistic)
    Select --> ConfirmSpill: No color available<br/>for optimistic node
    ConfirmSpill --> InsertSpills: Spill confirmed
    InsertSpills --> Build: Insert loads/stores,<br/>restart allocation

    Coalesce --> Weighting: Conservative coalescing<br/>(Briggs/George criterion)
    Weighting --> LoopWeight: Weighted spill costs<br/>(10^depth for loops)
    Weighting --> Remat: Rematerialization<br/>(recompute cheap values)
    Weighting --> Split: Live-range splitting<br/>(inner vs outer loop)
    LoopWeight --> [*]
    Remat --> [*]
    Split --> [*]

    state Build {
        [*] --> LiveRange: Live-variable analysis<br/>for each definition
        LiveRange --> InterGraph: Add edges between<br/>overlapping live ranges
        InterGraph --> SpillCost: Compute spill cost<br/>per node
    }

    state Chaitin["Chaitin's Algorithm"]
        Build --> Simplify
        Simplify --> Select
    end

    state Briggs["Briggs Improvement"]
        Simplify --> SpillMark: Push degree≥K nodes<br/>to stack optimistically
        SpillMark --> Select: Hope neighbors free<br/>a color later
    end

    state Coalesce {
        Aggressive: Merge all copy-related pairs
        Conservative: Merge only if safe
        Conservative --> BriggsCriterion: Merged node has<br/><K neighbors with deg≥K
        Conservative --> GeorgeCriterion: All high-degree<br/>neighbors already interfere
    }
